    "result": "```json\n{\n  \"answer\": \"10.22%\",\n  \"sql\": \"SELECT ROUND(100.0 * SUM(CASE WHEN f.rtg = 1 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) / COUNT(*), 2) AS pct_1star FROM fdbk_g2 f JOIN items_g2 i ON f.ref_id = i.ref_id WHERE LENGTH(f.body) > 500 AND i.prc <= 4000;\"\n}\n```\n\n**Reasoning:**\n- The three datasets map by dominant `main_cat`: **g1 = Office Products**, **g2 = Electronics**, **g3 = Musical Instruments** (verified by aggregation).\n- Electronics = `items_g2` / `fdbk_g2`, joined on `ref_id` (100% of reviews matched).\n- `prc` is in cents (`prc_usd = prc/100`, verified with 0 mismatches), so \"list price ≤ $40\" → `prc <= 4000` (equivalently `prc_usd <= 40`, identical result).\n- Review body longer than 500 characters → `LENGTH(body) > 500`; 1-star → `rtg = 1`.\n\nResult: 222 one-star reviews out of 2,172 qualifying reviews = **10.22%**.\n\nReusable findings (schema, group/category mapping, join keys, verified price-unit relationship, verified-vs-inferred distinctions) were saved to `memory/environment.md` with an index at `memory/MEMORY.md`.",
